# React + Convex client

`useQuery` is a subscription. Treat `undefined` as loading (skeletons), not as empty data.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
const messages = useQuery(api.messages.list, { channelId }) ?? [];

// ✅ GOOD
const messages = useQuery(api.messages.list, { channelId });
if (messages === undefined) return <Skeleton />;
```

- Gate the app with `Authenticated` / `Unauthenticated` / `AuthLoading` in `src/App.tsx`
- Use `ConvexAuthProvider` in `src/main.tsx` (not raw `ConvexProvider`)
- Sign-in form posts `FormData` with `email`, `password`, `flow`, and `name` on sign-up
- Debounce typing upserts (~300ms); clear typing on send, blur, and unmount
- Use shadcn pieces in `src/components/ui/`; put app components in `src/components/`
- Do not add React Router unless the user asks — channel selection stays in React state
